{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 19,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.815,
            0.049,
            0.861,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": "Area"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.089,
            0.847,
            0.127
          ],
          "content": "We have taken the length of one of the parallel sides as a. Let b be the length of the other parallel side."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.126,
            0.847,
            0.183
          ],
          "content": "Can the area of the trapezium be expressed in terms of a, b and h? To replace $x + y$ in the area expression with a and b, observe that $b = x + y + a.$ . Subtracting a from both sides, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.436,
            0.188,
            0.561,
            0.207
          ],
          "content": "x + y = b - a .",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.205,
            0.329,
            0.226
          ],
          "content": "Using this, we get"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.364,
            0.227,
            0.634,
            0.286
          ],
          "content": "{ \\mathrm { A r e a ~ W X Y Z } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } }   h ( b - a + 2 a ) , \\qquad { \\mathrm { A r e a ~ W X Y Z } } = { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } }   h ( b - a + 2 a ) .",
          "image_source": "images/page_19_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.279,
            0.262,
            0.299
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.215,
            0.312,
            0.777,
            0.34
          ],
          "content": "Area of a trapezium $\\scriptstyle { \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } \\times h e i g h t \\times s u m$ of the parallel sides."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.359,
            0.718,
            0.383
          ],
          "content": "？ Will this formula hold for a trapezium that looks like this?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.353,
            0.385,
            0.672,
            0.486
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.49,
            0.845,
            0.529
          ],
          "content": "There are different ways of approaching this, which are sketched below. Complete the arguments."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.535,
            0.536,
            0.555
          ],
          "content": "**Approach 1: Rectangle and Triangles**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.312,
            0.558,
            0.665,
            0.675
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.314,
            0.68,
            0.682,
            0.719
          ],
          "content": "Area ABCD = Area ABED + Area ∆BEC Area ABED = Area ABEF – Area ∆AFD"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.153,
            0.725,
            0.57,
            0.745
          ],
          "content": "**Approach 2: Parallelogram and Triangle**"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.337,
            0.746,
            0.657,
            0.858
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_15.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.45,
            0.86,
            0.589,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": "Draw BG ‖ AD"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.126,
            0.882,
            0.633,
            0.905
          ],
          "content": "? Will Approach 2 work for any type of trapezium?"
        },
